<title>AUSTRALIA: Australian Stocks to Watch Today - May 7.</title>
<headline>Australian Stocks to Watch Today - May 7.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Some Australian stocks to watch this morning:</p>
<p>*News Corp Ltd A$5.98 (+.11)</p>
<p>U.S. broker downgrades Rupert Murdoch's media empire to neutral from buy added it will be tough to follow box office performances of &quot;Independence day: and &quot;Star Wars&quot; and group's entrance into U.S. satellite TV business to drag on.</p>
<p>*RTZ Corp/CRA Ltd A$19.21 (+.11)</p>
<p>*Pasminco A$2.52 (+.10).</p>
<p>Century zinc project gets go ahead on Tuesday after Aboriginal claimants sign final agreement for A$1 billion project. RTZ-CRA has agreed to sell the Century project to Pasminco.</p>
<p>*Wesfarmers Ltd A$11.41 (+.215)</p>
<p>Wesfarmers posts 51 percent increase in net profit for nine months ended March 31 on Tuesday.</p>
<p>*Brambles Industries Ltd A$23.35 (+.05)</p>
<p>*Lend Lease Corp Ltd A$24.55 (+.55)</p>
<p>*Commonwealth Bank of Australia A$14.11 (+.12)</p>
<p>*Macquarie Bank Ltd A$9.22 (+.07)</p>
<p>Australia set to name successful bidders for the Melbounre, Perth and Brisbane airports today, each of the above companies are involved in various consortiums bidding for the airports.</p>
<p>*AAPC Ltd A$0.79 (+.02)</p>
<p>*Amalgamated Holdings Ltd A$7.01 (+.01)</p>
<p>Hotel groups may be affected by the New South Wales government's plans to impose a 10 percent &quot;bed tax&quot; on central Sydney from September this year. Sydney is one of Australia's most visited tourist spots.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
